KG42.register("clusters-bce0f5a7a73c0909cdd6e410",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v142-d-CL004","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","label":"Electricity charges for sharing, service-fee allocation, and ESP payment responsibilities","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"Electricity charges for sharing, service-fee allocation, and ESP payment responsibilities","market_meaning":"For participants' net energy exchanges, the applicable internal prices generate electricity charges or income; ESP charges service fees based on the energy actually shared and allocates them according to participants' contributions, while also bearing responsibilities related to payment balance and expense coverage. The existing chains provide the main charging relationships, but the treatment of zero exchange, fee conventions, and some input objects are not yet closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["settlement","coordination","pricing","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"This cluster uses net quantities and internal prices from the same operating period and version; non-scenario quantities do not automatically substitute for scenario quantities. The economic balance equation covers only 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, and the treatment of a zero denominator in service-fee allocation remains undetermined; surplus commodity quantities remain distinct from the quantities actually matched for sharing.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is defined by participants' monetary obligations and ESP's responsibilities for receipts and expenditures, connecting quantity, commodity, and price interfaces. Shared references provide only these interfaces and the relevant governance background; they do not turn the entire pricing solution, initiation of trading, or fairness disclosure into prerequisites for charging.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides electricity-charge or income terms, total service fees and their allocation, and requirements for economic balance and expense coverage."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides net quantities and aggregated supply and demand inputs within the same scope, while retaining the background of responsibilities related to payment balance, impartiality, and profit limits."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the selection of applicable internal prices according to net quantities and the design requirements for economic balance; it does not replace the missing complete billing accounts."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Describes the local photovoltaic sharing product involved in charging; actual billing quantities are still handled according to R008's definition of shared quantities."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-NP_i_h","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TSP_h","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TBP_h"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g02-E-12","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The service-fee and balance relationships use participants' net quantities and the area's total supply and demand, and can be connected to R001's aggregation inputs for the same time period and operating version. The symbols in R008 lack corresponding typed quantity objects, so only an interface is established, without fabricating same_quantity members."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C010","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C011"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23"],"rationale":"The price applicable to a prosumer selected by equation (16) enters that prosumer's monetary cost or income term; this interface retains the branches based on the sign of net quantities and does not treat economic inconvenience costs as fees paid to ESP."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON012","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::V::product.local_energy"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20"],"rationale":"The source connects local photovoltaic sharing activities with service fees charged and allocated according to shared quantities. Shareable surplus energy is only a product condition; billing quantities remain based on the actual amount of matched supply and demand, and all surplus energy cannot be directly used as the charging basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON013","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-39"],"rationale":"ESP's general balance and governance responsibilities supplement the specific charging and expense-coverage requirements. R001's dual balance responsibilities have a broader scope than R008's payment responsibilities, and the impartiality objective and profit limits are also not the same constraint; none are merged as duplicate formulas."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM010","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The entity receiving submissions, setting internal prices, and charging service fees is the same ESP; only a display representative is selected, while the different responsibilities and original objects are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM011","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The two locations reference the same internal pricing function in price selection and monetary payments; the price-formation conditions and payment expressions are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM012","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E18","v141-b-g04-e04"],"rationale":"Both locations are associated with the monetary payment function of the same sharing area; whether service fees are included in internal prices still requires separate clarification."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM013","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R008::V::product.local_energy"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::product.local_energy","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19"],"rationale":"Both locations refer to the local photovoltaic energy product within the sharing area; product-node identity does not mean that available surplus quantities equal the quantities actually shared and billed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G012","category":"math_incomplete","description":"When TSP^h and TBP^h are both zero, R008's total charging relationship gives a shared quantity of zero, but the individual allocation formula still contains 0/0. The existing chains provide no allocation treatment for periods with zero exchange, and the definition cannot be completed by independently assigning each household a zero share.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TSP_h","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TBP_h","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check and specify upstream the valid domain of the allocation formula and the treatment of zero exchange, while also checking its connection to the total amount; where the source provides no specification, undefined cases should be retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G013","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The adjusted energy consumption, PV output, applicable prices, fee results, and temporal scope in R008 remain primarily symbols within expressions, lacking complete typed objects and references. R001 can provide only net quantities and supply and demand aggregation; it cannot replace the missing scheduling chain, nor can original net quantities be directly equated with adjusted net quantities.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-NP_i_h","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C010","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C011","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-E-12","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Specify upstream the object to which each input and result belongs, their time periods, and operating versions, and provide formal references linking scheduling to payments; D retains only the current expressions and existing interfaces."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G014","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R006 states that the buying-price construction takes ESP's charges into account, whereas the balance of energy revenues and expenditures in R008-C007 has no explicit service-fee term, and R008 separately lists total service fees and their allocation. The existing chains do not specify whether service fees are included in or added to prices, nor do they form complete accounts that include service fees.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the respective accounting scopes of internal buying prices, service fees, and economic balance, and explain upstream how they are connected, to avoid double charging or mistaking energy balance for a complete payment balance that includes service fees."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G015","category":"math_incomplete","description":"β is described as a proportion, but the charging relationship acts directly on shared energy, and its units and monetary conversion convention are unspecified. Losses and organizational expenditures have no defined terms, and the profit limit has no numerical value; therefore, cost coverage or actual profit bounds cannot be verified from the existing chains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-beta","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-39"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Further check fee-rate units, monetary conventions, and the definitions of losses and expenditures; where the source provides no specification, retain the unspecified information and qualitative requirements without introducing case-specific fee rates, profit caps, or independently inferred cost terms."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G016","category":"unverified_source","description":"Charging, allocation, and economic balance are all based on the current unaudited B text; this cluster is only a partially assembled candidate available for manual inspection and does not constitute scientific confirmation of the payment rules.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the formulas, units, conditions, and fee conventions item by item, and examine all shared references; no independent source review or scientific review was conducted in this round."}]},"rule_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-20e312b579d3a493","COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-c6917f781ea3f39e","COMP-dddaa2edb4acd670","KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0"]});
